WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.870
If you want to hear about the true meaning
of Us and what everything represents then

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.880
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.570
Jordan Peele’s Us deals with a subterranean
society of doppelgangers who rises up to take

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.170
their place in the sunlight.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.910
The concept of literal underground societies
has been creepy and fascinating to me ever

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.490
since I found out that these so called “mole
people” actually exist.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.670
Yeah, this is a real thing -- and Peele’s
pairing of that with another creepy concept:

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.730
doppelgangers, is bound to leave moviegoers
looking something like this.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.300
The movie opens with a text card, telling
of the 1000s of miles of tunnels, unused subway

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.220
systems, service tunnels and mine shafts,
with no known purpose.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.670
The first image we see is the main character,
Addie, watching TV as a young girl in 1986.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.421
She’s watching the channel 11 news, one
of the many references to the number 11 seen

00:00:47.421 --> 00:00:48.421
throughout the move.

00:00:48.421 --> 00:00:50.820
We’ll come back to the meaning of 11 later
on.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.670
First, there are some easter eggs.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.989
On the side of the TV there are some VHS tapes,
and they may be there to honor some of the

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.780
films that helped inspire Us.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.940
One of them is C.H.U.D, a 1984 movie about
these subterranean monsters who abduct people.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.699
The relevance of that one should be pretty
obvious.

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:16.640
“And unlikely to bring anyone down there,
so they’re coming up.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.720
C.H.U.D!”

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.620
There’s also a tape of The Goonies, a 1985
kids film in which a group of children must

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:26.850
search for a pirates treasure in an underground
cavern -- just as the mother in Us must venture

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.060
underground to find her abducted son.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.030
The last tape I could make out was The Right
Stuff, which is a non-fiction movie about

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.890
the development of the space program, I’m
guessing it’s loosely related because venturing

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.100
underground is similar to space travel in
that you are setting out into an unknown frontier.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.330
The news on the TV goes to commercial ...and
she watches an ad for Hands Across America.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.360
The few seconds that this commercial is on-screen
are the key to understanding this entire film.

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:53.600
I understood everything a little bit better
when I went home and looked up what Hands

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.090
Across America actually was and what it stood
for.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.250
Hands across America was a charity event that
took place in 1986.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.790
Participants would donate $10 to reserve their
spot as Americans lined up and joined hands

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:08.520
for 15 minutes, theoretically creating a chain
from coast to coast across the mainland United

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.520
States.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.170
The goal of the event was to raise money and
awareness to help combat hunger and homelessness.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.410
When Addie goes to the Santa Cruz Beach Boardwalk
with her parents as a little girl, she’s

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.830
wearing a Hands Across America shirt -- and
it becomes one of her last solid memories

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.920
of the real world when she’s abducted by
the shadow people.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.590
At the carnival, her Dad wins her a Thriller
T-shirt, which she puts on over it.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:30.900
As they explore the boardwalk, Addie sees
various carnival activities that are significant.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.790
Her father wants to ride the roller coaster,
which he calls the Little Dipper.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.400
(In real life it’s called the Giant Dipper).

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.540
"Do the walk, the beach boardwalk.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.120
You can do the roller coaster you can do the
swim.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.060
Come on everybody you can walk right in."

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.620
This is either a reference to the idea that
Addie is going to be “dipping” or descending

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.970
into this underground world -- or another
way of looking at it is that the Big Dipper

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.840
and Little Dipper are constellations and while
those above the surface can see and observe

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.480
the stars, the tunnel dwelling doppelgangers
cannot.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.860
There are even a couple of lines throughout
the movie about the joy of being able to gaze

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:00.890
at the stars.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.450
They also walk by and notice some people playing
a whack-a-mole arcade game, a visual representation

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.580
of the people on the surface knocking those
who live underground back down, forcing them

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.800
to stay there.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.110
Before wandering off the boardwalk, Addie
sees a sign that says Jeremiah 11:11, and

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.840
this has multiple meanings.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.750
11:11 represents two sets of doubles.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.700
It’s also symmetrical, and it's the only
time on a digital clock that appears the exact

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.200
same in front of a mirror.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.819
This is assuming that there are slashes through
the zeroes, as there should be.

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:32.290
In culture 11:11 is often considered a lucky
or magic number, and I’ll be talking more

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.890
about the references to magic throughout this
video.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:40.830
But this sign specifically references Jeremiah
11:11, a biblical verse that reads: Therefore,

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:45.790
thus says the Lord, “Behold, I am bringing
disaster upon them that they cannot escape.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.120
Though they cry to me, I will not listen to
them.”

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.610
And this could be seen as a religious prediction
of the bloodshed that will be brought on by

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.580
the uprising of the doppelgangers.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.951
The last thing we see before Addie leaves
the boardwalk is her Dad playing Rock, Paper

00:03:56.951 --> 00:03:59.470
Scissors to settle a disagreement with her
Mom.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.540
Rock, Paper and Scissors each come back later
in the movie.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.230
The main weapon used by the shadow people
is scissors -- but the son, Jason, uses a

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:09.860
large rock to defeat one of them when they
flee to their friend’s house across the

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.860
lake.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.300
Then at the end of the movie, the fake version
of Addie uses a sharp fire poker to defeat

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.059
the original Addie who is wearing the red
jumpsuit, and holding the paper cutouts of

00:04:18.059 --> 00:04:21.199
the people linking hands, so this is kind
of a scissors beats paper moment.

00:04:21.199 --> 00:04:24.559
So when Addie walks off the boardwalk, she
goes from the bright lights of the carnival

00:04:24.559 --> 00:04:27.849
to the dark beach -- and there’s also a
moment at at the end of the movie when they

00:04:27.849 --> 00:04:30.599
are battling in the underground and they move
from the lit up part of the hallway into a

00:04:30.599 --> 00:04:32.120
stretch where the lights are off.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.550
The maze that Addie goes into on the beach
is called Shaman’s Vision Quest.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.119
The tagline is “find yourself”, and Addie
literally does find another version of herself

00:04:40.119 --> 00:04:41.119
in that maze.

00:04:41.119 --> 00:04:44.699
I also found it interesting that it starts
raining as soon as she goes in, because only

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:46.930
surface dwellers can experience rain.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.939
But if you’re a mole person and you’re
watching this, don’t feel bad, because at

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.900
least you guys don’t have buy sunscreen.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:56.680
So she wanders through the mirror maze, and
mirrors are another huge motif in this movie.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.270
The doppelgangers are mirror images of the
humans on the surface, and there are plenty

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.560
of examples of reflections as symbols for
the copies.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.449
She goes through one part in the forest where
she sees these distorted mirrors, and that

00:05:06.449 --> 00:05:10.349
may be tied to the fact that the son of the
underground family is distorted by the burn

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:11.660
marks on his face.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.960
There are three things that happen before
she runs into the doppelganger version of

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:15.960
herself.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.500
One: the lights go out; and two: all she can
see is the green exit signs reflected hundreds

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.949
of times in each mirror.

00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:25.529
Although there appear to be many exits, in
reality, she has no way out.

00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:28.750
And three: she hears the doppelganger version
of herself whistling.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.649
Remember those three things, because they’ll
be important later.

00:05:31.649 --> 00:05:35.419
And when that shadow girl does turn around
and see the original Addie, the scene cuts

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:39.699
away before we see her being abducted, and
the other girl switching shirts with her and

00:05:39.699 --> 00:05:40.719
going onto the surface.

00:05:40.719 --> 00:05:43.879
Now, I know I’m not supposed to have an
opinion, but in my opinion this would have

00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:47.810
been more convincing if we had seen her start
running, and then it jumpcut to her doppelganger

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.699
getting back to the parents on the boardwalk
so we think, oh OK she made it back alright,

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:55.379
and then in the reveal at the end of the movie,
it shows the shadow Addie running after and

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:58.099
dragging her back in before joining the parents
at the boardwalk.

00:05:58.099 --> 00:06:01.129
It would have made it a little bit less obvious
I think.

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:04.800
But instead it cuts to the shot of the rabbits
in cages, so let’s talk about the meaning

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:05.800
of rabbits.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.720
Rabbits are often seen as a symbol of reproduction
because they are known to reproduce very quickly.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.619
The people underground are reproductions of
the originals on the surface.

00:06:12.619 --> 00:06:16.520
With scissors sometimes being seen as the
image associated with a vasectomy, the surgery

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.199
that prevents you from producing offspring.

00:06:18.199 --> 00:06:22.069
But there’s also another idea that’s commonly
associated with rabbits: and that’s magic.

00:06:22.069 --> 00:06:25.699
The most classic magician’s trick involves
pulling a rabbit out of a hat.

00:06:25.699 --> 00:06:29.449
Well it just so happens that when the shadow
Addie grows up and has children, her son,

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:31.089
Jason, is interested in magic tricks.

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:33.449
He has a lot of peculiar things about him.

00:06:33.449 --> 00:06:35.539
At the start of the movie, he wears a Jaws
shirt.

00:06:35.539 --> 00:06:39.569
Perhaps this is because Jaws is a fellow beach-set
horror movie, but it could also have to do

00:06:39.569 --> 00:06:40.849
with his fascination with monsters.

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:44.449
He wears what I think is like a werewolf mask
think throughout the entire film.

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:49.039
Addie also has a daughter, Zora, who’s wearing
a shirt with a rabbit on it and seems to only

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:53.250
be interested in texting; and a husband, Gabe,
who participates in cringe-worthy dabs and

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.110
has a love for boats that's not shared by
any other family members.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:00.699
After meeting the family, we cut back to the
aftermath of Addie’s childhood boardwalk

00:07:00.699 --> 00:07:03.939
incident and discover that the doppelganger
version of her wouldn’t speak after being

00:07:03.939 --> 00:07:07.770
found by her parents -- who of course have
no idea it’s not the real her, and think

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.419
it’s some kind of PTSD.

00:07:09.419 --> 00:07:11.620
She sees them meet with the doctor through
a mirror.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.069
I think the reason that she doesn’t speak
is because when the doppels come up from underground

00:07:15.069 --> 00:07:18.159
it takes them some time to adjust to breathing
our fresh oxygen.

00:07:18.159 --> 00:07:22.119
She’s unable to speak properly until her
lungs have adapted to the fresh air.

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:25.770
That’s why when the original Addie comes
back up to try to take over the surface, she

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.140
sounds like this:

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.379
"Be careful."

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:37.879
There’s further proof later on, when the
family flees to the other house and Gabe’s

00:07:37.879 --> 00:07:41.999
friend’s wife is seen screaming and laughing
in the mirror, but no sound comes out.

00:07:41.999 --> 00:07:45.899
So as the family settles into the beach house,
there are a few pieces to note around the

00:07:45.899 --> 00:07:46.899
house.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:50.419
There’s a shot of a spider crawling on the
table under a toy spider, an early clue that

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:55.110
the real Addie is crawling beneath, and it’s
the fake one that is on top -- on the surface.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.770
This imagery also connects with the song that
the doppelgangers whistle when they arrive

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.539
at the house: the itsy-bitsy spider.

00:08:01.539 --> 00:08:05.039
She expresses that she doesn’t want to go
to the Santa Cruz Beach, not because she was

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:08.499
traumatized there as a child, but because
she knows that she’ll be in close proximity

00:08:08.499 --> 00:08:11.649
to the tunnel network and she’s afraid something
could happen.

00:08:11.649 --> 00:08:16.010
Her walls are covered with artwork of Alvin
Ailey, a known dance choreographer, and at

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.209
the end of the movie, it’s revealed that
it was her dance recital when she realized

00:08:19.209 --> 00:08:21.839
she was in control and she could be on the
surface.

00:08:21.839 --> 00:08:25.770
It’s as the doctor told Addie’s parents,
the best they can do for her is allow her

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.580
to draw, write and dance.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.319
Jason enjoys playing inside the cabinet / closet.

00:08:30.319 --> 00:08:34.329
The door automatically locks when closed,
so he props it up with a little toy ambulance

00:08:34.329 --> 00:08:35.329
thing.

00:08:35.329 --> 00:08:38.419
It’s literally his lifeline, and also Gabe
and Zora are saved at the end of the movie

00:08:38.419 --> 00:08:41.399
when the come across a real ambulance and
get supplies.

00:08:41.399 --> 00:08:45.220
Inside the closet I spotted games like Guess
Who?, Magic and Candyland.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:49.850
Guess Who? is literally a game where two identical
sets of people are lined up on opposite sides,

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.330
not that different than the way this world
is setup.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:56.580
Magic is obviously a part of Jason’s passion
for magic tricks, and Candy Land...

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.860
I guess there’s a version where the characters
are all rabbits…?

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.550
But I didn’t have that one as a kid.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:01.540
I had this one.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:06.680
The mom finds a rabbit doll in a drawer and
we see she’s affected by it, but it isn’t

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.420
entirely clear why -- it’s because it reminds
her of when she was trapped underground until

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.740
she made the switch.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:13.870
So they all get in the car and go to the beach.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.990
Zora mentions something about how she thinks
the government is putting fluoride in the

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.170
water so that the government can control us,
a flight allusion to the fact that they could

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.269
all be controlled by those living underground.

00:09:22.269 --> 00:09:26.870
As they’re about to arrive, a dead body
is wheeled onto another ambulance, and this

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.910
guy is holding another Jeremiah 11:11 sign.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.440
This signals the beginning of everything that
happened that day at the boardwalk repeating

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:36.619
itself leading up to the arrival of the “tethered”
family.

00:09:36.619 --> 00:09:41.100
Their long shadows as they walk onto the beach
signify that the shadow people are drawing

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.100
near.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.470
The Shaman’s Vision Quest is now Merlin’s
Forest (another magic reference).

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:49.290
Gabe’s friend Josh bickers with his wife,
just as Addie’s parents did on the boardwalk

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.640
all those years ago.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.790
By the way, they have twin daughters, another
example of mirrorism.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:58.540
They even have a moment where they say the
same thing at the same and then both jinx

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.180
and double jinks each other.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.160
Just like 11:11, this is an example of a pair
of doubles.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.910
The scene with them later at the house pays
homage to Grady twins from the Shining.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:11.100
I’m pretty sure the Shining has come like
3 videos in a row now -- and it actually comes

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.920
up again later in this video.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.760
Jason wanders off to go to the bathroom and
sees the guy T-posing, or at least that’s

00:10:24.769 --> 00:10:27.740
what it looks like, and I think this is the
first guy to come up from underground and

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.240
start the new Hands Across America chain.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.259
His Mom freaks out when he’s gone, because
she knows about the subterranean society and

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:36.470
she’s afraid that Jason could be abducted.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:40.640
When they get home that evening, Gabe is watching
the Giants game and if you listen to the audio

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.579
in the background, you’ll hear the score
is tied 11-11.

00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:47.569
Not long after, when they tell the son to
go to bed, the clock reads 11:11 PM.

00:10:47.569 --> 00:10:51.360
There’s also a LEGO ferris wheel in the
boy’s room to reference to rides at the

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.330
Beach Boardwalk, and picture of Merlin on
his bedroom wall.

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:58.089
He’s also wearing a tuxedo shirt which makes
him look like a magician in uniform.

00:10:58.089 --> 00:11:02.089
His mother gets worried when she realizes
he’s drawn a picture of the T-posing man

00:11:02.089 --> 00:11:05.870
from the beach, because she possibly realizes
what this is.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:09.779
In the bedroom, she stares into her reflection
in the window as she expresses her concerns

00:11:09.779 --> 00:11:10.779
to Gabe.

00:11:10.779 --> 00:11:14.689
She tells him it feels like a black cloud
is hanging over her and she feels a storm

00:11:14.689 --> 00:11:18.410
coming, very similar to how it started raining
when Addie entered the mirror maze all those

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.470
years ago.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:23.810
Then the three things that happened back then
happen again: the power goes out, all exits

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.709
are compromised and whistling can be heard
from the doppelgangers.

00:11:26.709 --> 00:11:31.279
When we first see them, they are holding hands
like the Hands Across America commercial.

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:34.450
The shadow people take over the house and
explain that they basically don’t have good

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:38.500
lives down below and they want their time
in the sun, they want to be untethered from

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.510
the bodies of the original family.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.649
Each character goes off and battles the shadow
version of themselves.

00:11:43.649 --> 00:11:47.660
The struggle between the two mothers is symbolic,
because Addie forces her doppelganger into

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:52.060
the glass table and we see it crack, representing
the barrier between the two versions of that

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:53.800
character being broken.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:57.149
Each character is able to fight off the other
version of them and together, they flee for

00:11:57.149 --> 00:12:00.190
Josh’s family’s house for help, but by
the time they get there, they’ve already

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.100
been taken over by doppelgangers.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:06.319
One of Josh’s last actions is telling the
virtual assistant to put on “Good Vibrations”

00:12:06.319 --> 00:12:07.319
by The Beach Boys.

00:12:07.319 --> 00:12:10.379
The lyrics describe Addie’s fascination
with the world on the surface.

00:12:10.379 --> 00:12:14.769
“I love the colorful clothes she wears
And the way the sunlight plays upon her hair.

00:12:14.769 --> 00:12:18.470
I hear the sound of a gentle word,
On the wind that lifts her perfume through

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:19.470
the air.”

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.750
The next verse describes shadow Addie sensing
the underground uprising.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.689
“Close my eyes,
She’s somehow closer now.”

00:12:25.689 --> 00:12:29.519
The other song that plays has lyrics that
are little more on the nose.

00:12:29.519 --> 00:12:32.380
“F the police straight from the underground.”

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:35.700
This literally describes what happens, where
the cops are unable to help them because so

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.300
many people are attacked from underground.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.149
After defeating the copies of the neighbors,
we get that second The Shining reference I

00:12:42.149 --> 00:12:43.149
promised.

00:12:43.149 --> 00:12:45.339
Jason just gets done saying something about
there being too many twins when they turn

00:12:45.339 --> 00:12:48.519
on the news and discover these people are
supposedly coming out of the sewers.

00:12:48.519 --> 00:12:52.980
The time is displayed on the bottom left corner
of the news overlay, it’s now 2:37 -- a

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.499
reference to Room 237 in The Shining.

00:12:55.499 --> 00:12:59.350
The family drives away in the neighbor’s
new car and they eventually encounter Jason’s

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.620
doppelganger with the mask again.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.080
He’s luring them into a gasolene trap.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.540
This part is a little bit confusing, but I
think what’s happening is that the two kids,

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:10.560
Jason and Zora have the power to control the
red suit doppelgangers, because they are both

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.040
half shadow people themselves.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:17.209
So it would appear that Jason uses this power
to walk backwards and drive his creepy doppelganger

00:13:17.209 --> 00:13:18.709
back into the flames.

00:13:18.709 --> 00:13:22.279
He saves his family by doing so, but it also
leads to him being kidnapped.

00:13:22.279 --> 00:13:26.910
We also get a look at a huge group of doppelgangers
linking hands along the coast, and the T-posing

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:31.269
guy from before has 11:11 written on his forehead,
which predicts more trouble.

00:13:31.269 --> 00:13:34.740
So Jason’s mother goes down into the forest
maze to try to rescue him.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:39.160
Then the two versions of Addie face off underground,
I’m going to put everything together and

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:42.740
talk about what this movie actually means,
and what it’s trying to say.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:43.930
So don’t go anywhere.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.740
Or someone will drag you underground.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.600
And you will never come back.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:59.220
So during the final showdown, Addie explains
her three decade plan, how after she was abducted

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:03.420
by the mole people, she basically put together
her own Hands Across America campaign.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:07.149
She explains that whoever created them was
able to duplicate their bodies, but not their

00:14:07.149 --> 00:14:11.249
souls, which I believe is why they are violent
to the surface dwellers, cause only one of

00:14:11.249 --> 00:14:13.100
them can inhabit that soul.

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:16.570
Everything they have down below is just a
crappy simulation of real real life, but in

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:20.579
spite of that, they are human too, they are
made up of flesh and blood just like those

00:14:20.579 --> 00:14:24.879
on the surface and they deserve and equal
experience and should not be overlooked.

00:14:24.879 --> 00:14:27.850
That leads into what I think Us is trying
to say as a movie.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:32.660
The people on the surface represent everyday
people leading normal lives in developed countries.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.120
Sometimes, they don’t fully appreciate what
they have.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.660
In the scene where the shadow family breaks
into the house, Addie describes the differences

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.829
between the lives of those on the surface
and those underground.

00:14:41.829 --> 00:14:47.660
The surface people get warm meals, while the
subterranean society has to eat cold raw rabbit.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:52.260
The kids on the surface get nice toys, but
the toys underground are cold and spiky.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:56.089
She also describes the differences between
the two seemingly parallel families.

00:14:56.089 --> 00:14:59.939
She tells the story of the girl who had a
shadow, how they were connected; tethered

00:14:59.939 --> 00:15:00.939
together.

00:15:00.939 --> 00:15:01.980
The girl married a prince.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.620
Although the family sees Gabe is sometimes
jealous of his friend’s car, house and boat

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.490
constantly one upping him, a family such as
the doppel family would be happy with what

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:11.490
he has.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:14.269
She also describes how the girl in the story
gave birth to a son.

00:15:14.269 --> 00:15:18.490
Jason is sometimes criticised for being a
bit strange and wearing a monster mask, but

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:23.259
the shadow girl gave birth to an actual monster
who acts like a real beast and needs to wear

00:15:23.259 --> 00:15:25.000
a mask to cover up his scars.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.720
The idea is to be happy with what you have
and not lose sight of the fact that there

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.399
are less fortunate people among you…

00:15:30.399 --> 00:15:32.709
maybe even living below you.

00:15:32.709 --> 00:15:37.240
Just as Hands Across America was organized
all those years ago -- the people living underground

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:42.639
revive it in a much bigger way to bring attention
to the cold, sad lives that those born underground

00:15:42.639 --> 00:15:45.350
are subjected to by staging their own movement.

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:49.360
The final shot of the movie is a huge sweeping
overhead shot showing the massive amount of

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.889
people in red jumpsuits forming a Hands Across
America chain, the shot is very reminiscent

00:15:53.889 --> 00:15:58.339
of the 1986 commercial that was shown to us
at the very beginning of the movie.

00:15:58.339 --> 00:16:02.050
Of course, if you have another interpretation
of this movie, or any other things I might

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.250
have missed in this video, be sure to let
me know in the comments, and check out the

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:08.350
playlist on the left to see all the things
you might have missed in the trailers for

00:16:08.350 --> 00:16:10.680
the upcoming horror movie Pet Sematary.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:15.870
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.689
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:16:19.689 --> 00:16:22.049
Assuming we both survive.

